+### Screen width
+
+`--width 240|256|288` (or `3:2`, `16:10`, `16:9`; or `TBS_WIDTH`) picks the
+screen's width at start-up; 160 lines always. The game reads it as
+`DISPLAY_WIDTH`, which is a variable in the native build. What follows it:
+
+- The field's layers draw into 64-tile-wide maps (`native/wide_map.h`): a
+  text background with BGCNT bit 13 set (the affine wrap bit, unused by text
+  backgrounds) reads its map from `gNativeWideMaps` instead of VRAM.
+- The camera centres on the leader across the whole width
+  (`FIELD_VIEW_FOCUS_X`, `FIELD_VIEW_WIDTH`).
+- Window registers keep 8-bit edges; `WIN_RANGE` writes a right edge past
+  255 as 240, and the display takes a right edge of 240 or more as the
+  screen's edge (the battle backdrop's window had wrapped to 32 pixels).
+
+Not yet: the window layer (menus, messages, the battle HUD) is still 32
+tiles wide, so at 288 its boxes wrap and the battle command row crashes.
+256 plays through.
+
 The headless build takes the arena repo's smoke scripts (`scripts/smoke/*.txt`:
 `wait`, `press`, `tap`, `mash`, `include`, `shot`, `peek`, `poke`) and writes
 the shots as PNG files:
